# Cache refreshes (sysusers, tmpfiles, udev, desktop, icon, user units) are all
# handled by the standard pacman hooks, so these functions only print.
post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
GreenBoost Gaming Suite installed.

  1. Memory-tiering group.  The 'greenboost' group was created so that a game
     launch can flag gaming_mode in the GreenBoost kernel module.  Add yourself
     and log back in for it to take effect:
         sudo usermod -aG greenboost "$USER"

     The kernel module itself comes from the optional 'greenboost' package.

  2. Fan-curve daemon (optional, per user):
         systemctl --user enable --now gb-gaming-fan-daemon
     It idles until you load a profile in the GUI.

  3. Steam compatibility tool.  "GreenBoost Proton" and
     "GreenBoost Proton Experimental" are installed in
     /usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d.  If Steam does not list them in
     Properties -> Compatibility, restart Steam, or point it at the directory:
         export STEAM_EXTRA_COMPAT_TOOLS_PATHS=/usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d

  4. The Vulkan layer is implicit and only activates when GREENBOOST_VULKAN=1.
     The launcher sets it where a game is involved; the GUI itself deliberately
     does not (otherwise Steam and everything it spawns would inherit it too).

  5. NVIDIA + Wayland: the GUI would otherwise die at startup with
         Gdk-Message: Error 71 (Protocol error) dispatching to Wayland display.
     so the launcher sets WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 for the webview
     only.  If the window still comes up blank or half-drawn, try one of:
         WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE=1 greenboost-gaming
         __NV_DISABLE_EXPLICIT_SYNC=1 greenboost-gaming
     The second keeps GPU acceleration, but the NVIDIA libraries read it, so
     Steam and the games you launch from this Suite inherit it too and may
     show buffer artefacts.  Once a driver/GTK fix lands, opt out of the
     built-in one with GREENBOOST_WEBKIT_GPU=1.

  Start the suite with "greenboost-gaming", or from the application grid.
  Docs: /usr/share/doc/greenboost-gaming-suite/README.md
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
GreenBoost Gaming Suite removed.

User data was left alone on purpose:
  ~/.config/greenboost-gaming/            per-game overrides, GPU profiles, global settings
  ~/.local/share/greenboost/              session history and the dataflux event log
  ~/.local/share/greenboost-gaming/       downloaded DLSS/Streamline libraries
  ~/.steam/*/compatibilitytools.d/        any GreenBoost Proton you deployed by hand

If you added yourself to the 'greenboost' group, remove it with:
  sudo gpasswd -d "$USER" greenboost
EOF
}
